{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLpkPeLVLw4k34PJnDJq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it in `_print_Mul` in `sympy/printing/latex.py`. The LaTeX tests in `sympy/printing/tests/test_latex.py` pass (170 passed, 2 expected failures).\n\n**Cause:** with `evaluate=False`, the parser turns `1/10` into `Mul(1, Pow(10, -1))`. The printer has a rule for unevaluated products that start with `1`: it prints every factor literally so the `1` stays visible. That rule caught these too, so `1/10` came out as `1 \\cdot \\frac{1}{10}` and `1/1` as `1 \\cdot 1^{-1}`.\n\n**Fix:** a product of exactly `1` and `something**-1` now skips that rule and is printed as a normal fraction. Other unevaluated products, like `Mul(1, 2)`, still print in full (`1 \\cdot 2`).\n\nOutput after the fix:\n\n| Input | LaTeX |\n|---|---|\n| `(1/10)**(1/20)` | `\\left(\\frac{1}{10}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{20}}` |\n| `(1/1)**(1/1)` | `\\left(\\frac{1}{1}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{1}}` |\n| `(10/1)**(20/1)` | `\\left(\\frac{10}{1}\\right)^{\\frac{20}{1}}` (unchanged) |\n| `(2)**(3/2)` | `2^{\\frac{3}{2}}` (unchanged) |\n| `(-2)**(3/2)` | `\\left(-2\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}` (unchanged) |\n\nThe first two now match the format of the cases the issue lists as expected."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1313,"cache_read_input_tokens":22430,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1313},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2e411df-3095-4e87-b9d5-467c66e025fe","uuid":"c37ebcbe-d61d-43a4-b7b1-67d3740396ac","timestamp":"2026-11-24T00:41:52.744Z","request_id":"req_011ChLpkPW9Ne8Dt3cs8iffi"}
